{
  "title": "Serum urate improves source-cycle HbA1c prediction but fails frozen transfer to a second NHANES cycle",
  "abstract": "In complete-case NHANES adults aged 20\u201379, adding a serum-urate spline and urate\u2013glucose interaction lowered 2005\u201306 cross-validated HbA1c MSE by 0.008459, but did not improve frozen prediction in 2007\u201308 (n=4874; weighted MSE 0.281627 baseline versus 0.291741 augmented; paired gain -0.010114, target-PSU 95% interval -0.022697 to 0.002679). This is failure to confirm incremental predictive benefit in a second survey sample, not proof of no urate\u2013glycemia association or universal harm.",
